ting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-b & =0 \\\\ 8x & =b \\\\ x & =\\frac{b}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the point that must be excluded from the domain is $x=\\frac{b}{8}.$ \n\nOn the other hand, we can see that $x=5$ is excluded from the domain. Equating this to $\\frac{b}{8},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{8} & =5 \\\\ b & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243268 13194139533637 true] [17592186243267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533637 true] [17592186243267 1041 "field-1" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243268 13194139533637 true] [17592186243267 1110 #uuid "cd0ceac2-f057-583c-ac45-c9e60c17e6e9" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243268 1034 "40" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533637 true] [17592186243268 1111 #uuid "45dc1dfe-8a15-547c-bb97-6d6d6a43e17d" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243269 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243270 13194139533637 true] [17592186243269 1089 "q-276641" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243269 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533637 true] [17592186243269 1100 "If the domain of the function $q(x)=\\frac{4}{9x-k}$ is $(-\\infty ,\\frac{1}{3})\\cup (\\frac{1}{3},\\infty ),$ then $k=${{field-1}}." 13194139533637 true] [17592186243269 1113 #uuid "e4a62a31-f3c1-5d25-9577-7c2ed7a8cdeb" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243269 1138 false 13194139533637 true] [17592186243269 1145 "A reciprocal function is defined for all values of $x$ except for those that make the denominator zero. So, to find the domain, we must exclude all values that make the denominator zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-k & =0 \\\\ 9x & =k \\\\ x & =\\frac{k}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the point that must be excluded from the domain is $x=\\frac{k}{9}.$ \n\nOn the other hand, we can see that $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ is excluded from the domain. Equating this to $\\frac{k}{9},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{9} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ k & =\\frac{9}{3} \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243271 13194139533637 true] [17592186243270 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533637 true] [17592186243270 1041 "field-1" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243270 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243271 13194139533637 true] [17592186243270 1110 #uuid "81c79035-1d92-5c39-a73d-d13db555cead" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243271 1034 "3" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533637 true] [17592186243271 1111 #uuid "23ee9fe3-a3ee-599f-8c30-7d88b46b1090" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243272 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243273 13194139533637 true] [17592186243272 1089 "q-276643" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243272 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533637 true] [17592186243272 1100 "If the domain of the function $f(x)=\\frac{10}{kx+4}$ is $(-\\infty ,-\\frac{1}{2})\\cup (-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ),$ then $k=${{field-1}}." 13194139533637 true] [17592186243272 1113 #uuid "2c4479f1-35eb-5eb4-98de-700106f681d6" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243272 1138 false 13194139533637 true] [17592186243272 1145 "A reciprocal function is defined for all values of $x$ except for those that make the denominator zero. So, to find the domain, we must exclude all values that make the denominator zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kx+4 & =0 \\\\ kx & =-4 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{4}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the point that must be excluded from the domain is $x=-\\frac{4}{k}.$ \n\nOn the other hand, we can see that $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ is excluded from the domain. Equating this to $-\\frac{4}{k},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{k} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{4}{k} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533637 true] [17592186243273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243274 13194139533637 true] [17592186243273 1040 #edb/ref 1759218604